The files 0.pgm to 9.pgm in this directory are images from the test set of
the MNIST database of handwritten digits, by Yann LeCun, Corinna Cortes and
Christopher J. C. Burges. MNIST was built from NIST Special Database 3 and
Special Database 1.
Source: http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/

Each file is the first image of its digit in the MNIST test set (test indices
3, 2, 1, 18, 4, 8, 11, 0, 61 and 7 for digits 0 to 9). The only change is the
conversion from the MNIST IDX format to binary PGM (P5) by export.py.

